/// Catalina — a socket server: an acceptor pool handing each connection to a
/// handler process. A port of Thousand Island.
///
/// `start:` takes the `ServerConfig` options and answers the running
/// `ServerSupervisor`. Each call starts an independent server, so a node can
/// run several; `srv stop` stops one and leaves the others running. With a
/// `{#name, n}` entry in `supervisorOptions` the server is registered under
/// `n` (from a bounded set of names, ADR 0079) and `ServerSupervisor named:
/// n` finds it.
///
/// ## Examples
/// ```beamtalk
/// srv := (Catalina start: #{#port => 0, #handler => EchoHandler}) unwrap
/// srv listenerInfo     // => Result ok: {{0, 0, 0, 0}, 54321}
/// srv connectionPids   // => Result ok: #()
/// srv stop
/// ```
sealed typed Object subclass: Catalina

  /// Start a server. `Result error:` if the options are invalid or the
  /// server cannot start (the port is taken, say).
  class sealed start: options :: Dictionary -> Result =>
    configured := Result tryDo: [ServerConfig fromOptions: options]
    configured isError ifTrue: [^configured]
    config := configured value
    name := Erlang proplists get_value: #name with: config supervisorOptions
    name =:= #undefined ifTrue: [
      Result tryDo: [ServerSupervisor spawnWith: config]
    ] ifFalse: [ServerSupervisor spawnWith: config as: name]
